<!--
  Sample policy for an API proxy that wants to call the
  ISAM-WSTrust-TokenExchange shared flow, e.g. attached in PreFlow
  before the proxy's own target logic.

  Optional: set compressSaml as a flow variable before this step to override
  the KVM default for this one request, e.g. via an AssignMessage/JS step:

    <AssignVariable>
        <Name>compressSaml</Name>
        <Value>true</Value>
    </AssignVariable>

  After this step runs:
    - The shared flow has already set request headers X-SAML-Assertion
      (base64, zipped or plain per compressSaml), X-SAML-Assertion-Compressed
      (true/false), and X-SAML-Subject-Id, so if your target just needs
      those forwarded as-is, there's nothing further to do.
    - The following flow variables are also available if you'd rather read
      them directly instead of relying on the headers this shared flow set:
        isam.rstr.assertion.xml            raw <saml:Assertion> XML
        isam.exchanged.subject.id          SAML subject (NameID)
        isam.exchanged.assertion.notBefore / .notOnOrAfter
        saml.assertion.output              base64 output (zipped or plain)
        saml.assertion.compressed          bool
        saml.signature.valid               bool, true by the time this step
                                            returns, since RF-SAML-Signature-Invalid
                                            would otherwise have raised a fault
        saml.signature.cert.subject / .issuer / .thumbprint

  Any fault before this step completes (missing config/bearer token, both
  ISAM hosts down, SOAP fault, invalid signature) propagates up as a raised
  fault; handle it in this proxy's DefaultFaultRule/FaultRules as needed.
-->
<FlowCallout name="FC-ISAM-WSTrust-TokenExchange">
    <DisplayName>FC ISAM WSTrust Token Exchange</DisplayName>
    <SharedFlowBundle>ISAM-WSTrust-TokenExchange</SharedFlowBundle>
</FlowCallout>
